    "title": "2025 Roundup: Climate Change - NewsBreak",
    "text": "28 minutes ago Support for climate change and environmental resilience saw big gains in 2025, although philanthropic efforts were broadly affected by U.S. government funding and policy changes that limited or discontinued American participation in several global initiatives, including the United Nations-led COP 30 climate change conference in Belém, Brazil. This year’s top stories include Bill Gates’ call for a change in the way the sector battles climate change, Bloomberg Philanthropies’ response to the U.S. decision to pull out of the Paris Agreement, and billions of dollars mobilized by major grantmakers to address Sustainable Development Goals. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
